<p>To counteract the dynamic forces of highway travel, high-tensile ratchet lashing is employed. These straps are anchored to reinforced points on the carrier frame and are tightened to a specific torque specification. This creates a rigid tension that prevents any lateral or longitudinal movement.</p>
<p>The ratchet mechanism allows for fine-tuned adjustments, ensuring that the bike is secured without damaging fairings or delicate components. This multi-point restraint system is critical for preventing vibration-induced wear and accidental shifts during high-speed transit.</p>
